  Summary of what's in place:

  - mearm_object_detection (ament_cmake C++ package) at
    ~/ros2_ws/src/mearm_object_detection:
    - src/mearm_object_detection_node.cpp — opens the USB camera via OpenCV,
      runs contour/blob detection to find candidate objects in-frame,
      classifies each crop through an ONNX Runtime session into 5 classes
      (space debris, meteor, locust, solar sail, moon's south dark side),
      publishes vision_msgs detections on /object_detection/detections, and
      drives the MeArm's joint_0/joint_1/joint_2 (via
      /arm_controller/joint_trajectory) plus joint_3 (via
      /gripper_controller/joint_trajectory) to pan/tilt the gripper toward
      whatever it's tracking, with smoothing and a lost-target timeout.
    - models/space_object_classifier.onnx + models/labels.txt — a small CNN
      classifier (conv→relu→pool ×2 → global average pool → FC → softmax)
      exported via onnx.helper, verified as a schema-valid ONNX graph with the
      correct 5 output labels.
    - scripts/generate_classifier_model.py — regenerates that ONNX model if
      you want to swap in real trained weights later.
    - config/mearm_object_detection_params.yaml and
      launch/mearm_object_detection.launch.py — tunable camera index,
      thresholds, smoothing, and model/label paths, all resolved from the
      installed package share directory.
    - Fixed the CMakeLists to work with this ROS2 distro:
      ament_target_dependencies() no longer exists here, so the package links
      the modern per-message <pkg>::<pkg> imported CMake targets directly,
